# Writing Code

- Write concise, minimal code. Prefer fewer lines over verbose implementations.
- Never leave dead code, commented-out code, or unused variables/imports/functions.
- Remove any code that is no longer called or reachable before finishing a task.
- Write tests for all code. Aim for > 75% test coverage. Flag all changes made to existing tests.

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — commented-out code and unused import
import { unusedHelper } from './helpers';
// const legacy = computeLegacy(data);

// ✅ GOOD — remove unused imports and dead code
export function process(data: Data) {
  return transform(data);
}
```

When changing behavior, add or update Vitest tests (e.g. `*.test.ts`, `*.test.tsx`) alongside the change. In your summary, call out any edits to existing tests.
